# BAWAAL Arena Challenge Architecture (LOCKED baseline)

High-performance stealth-black sports network centered on **asynchronous 1v1 video battles**.
Further work builds on this contract — do not regress the single video Arena feed, slim FACEOFF hub, BATTLES open callouts, 1-tap challenge camera, or post-record teardown.

## Core mechanics

- Side-by-side battle cards: **YOU / opener on the left** vs **challenger on the right** (`ArenaFeed.js` `BattleCard`).
- Open challenges: left = host benchmark (`@YOU`), right = empty RESPOND slot until athletes reply.
- Primary surface: `ArenaFeed.js` (Arena tab). Camera: `UniversalCamera.tsx`.

## Single video Arena feed (`ArenaFeed.js`)

- Main Arena is a **clutter-free cinematic video feed** — no dual-segment toggle, no horizontal category pill scroller, **no in-feed floating alert ticker/toast**.
- Header: **ARENA** + top-right **FACEOFF** action.
- Cold-start shows the unified feed (Sparks, reels, high-engagement + battles).

## FACEOFF hub (scores + sports only)

- Tap **FACEOFF** opens a dedicated hub containing:
  1. Live sports scores ticker (`ScoresSportsPanel` — B&W monochromatic).
  2. Sports category grid (locked taxonomy).
- Do **not** reintroduce Open Callouts / challenges lists inside FACEOFF.

## BATTLES tab — Open Callouts

- `BattlesScreen.js` hosts **Active Battles** and **Open Callouts**.
- Open Callouts use two categories (`src/utils/faceoffCallout.js`):
  - **OPEN CHALLENGES** — performance, benchmark, or 1v1 action callouts.
  - **TIPS & BREAKDOWNS** — technique, advice, or form-check requests.
- UI panel: `src/components/OpenCalloutsPanel.js`.

## Sports category taxonomy (FACEOFF grid)

Canonical order in `src/utils/sportCategory.js` → `BAWAAL_SPORT_TAXONOMY` (do not rename/reorder; see `bawaal-sport-taxonomy-locked.mdc`):

1. ALL  
2. CRICKET  
3. FOOTBALL  
4. GYM  
5. KABADDI  
6. COMBAT  
7. THROTTLE  
8. WAVE & BLADE  
9. COURT KINGS  
10. SKY & SUMMIT  
11. OTHERS  

- Blueprint shorthand “THROTTLE | WAVE & BLADE” / “SKY & SUMMIT / OTHERS” maps to **separate** grid cells — never collapse labels.

## Challenge creation & camera (1-tap)

- **`+ BATTLE` FAB** and Battles **LAUNCH ARENA CHALLENGE** → **single tap** into `UniversalCamera` challenge / opener mode (`captureOpenerOnly` / `isArenaOpenChallenge` via `MainTabs.openArenaChallenge`).
- Do **not** insert a blocking confirmation sheet before the camera.
- After opener capture, publish path may reopen Create Arena Challenge only for Publish — never block the initial camera open.
- Publish: upload opener to Supabase Storage + insert `arena_challenges` (`src/services/arenaChallengeService.js`), then **prepend** to Arena (`pushOpenChallenge`) with active **RESPOND**; BATTLES Open Callouts also surface new open cards.

## Post-recording stability (`UniversalCamera.tsx`)

- Await native `stopRecording` / in-flight `recordAsync` **before** React state flips or navigation.
- Keep **`RECORDING_TEARDOWN_MS = 200`** (+ preview handshake) so expo-camera / expo-av release the hardware lock.
- Use `isProcessing` / `isFinalizingClip` gates; clear preview players and recording refs on unmount / `safeNavigateHome`.
- Do not remount/unmount `CameraView` mid-flush.

## Scalability vision (do not regress when adding)

- Main card remains the primary 1v1 comparison.
- Future: expandable horizontal **Responses Tray** of mini split-screen thumbnails to swap active challengers into full clarity — add alongside this chrome, do not replace the dual-pane card or RESPOND CTA.

## Re-hydration prompt (maintain)

Load project context for BAWAAL: Keep the main Arena surface as a single clutter-free cinematic video feed with ARENA + FACEOFF in the header and no in-feed alert ticker. FACEOFF hosts only live scores and the sports category grid. Open Callouts (OPEN CHALLENGES | TIPS & BREAKDOWNS) live on the BATTLES tab alongside Active Battles. Keep the 1-tap challenge creation route to `UniversalCamera.tsx` active, preserving the asynchronous video teardown delay (200ms) to prevent native camera memory unmount crashes.

